#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Video Downloader Ultra native messaging host.

Protocol: 4-byte little-endian length prefix + UTF-8 JSON, on stdin/stdout.

Requests:
  {"req": <id>, "action": "ping"}                      -> {"req", "ok": true, "ytdlp": bool, "ffmpeg": bool}
  {"req": <id>, "action": "probe", "url": "..."}       -> {"req", "ok": true, "meta": {...}, "formats": [...], "subs": {}, "autoSubs": {}}
  {"req": <id>, "action": "download", "url": "...",
   "selection": {...}}                                  -> {"req", "ok": true, "queueId": <id>}; the job either
                                                          starts immediately or joins a FIFO queue and runs when
                                                          the active job finishes (done, error, or cancel)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "cancel"}                     -> {"req", "ok": true} (terminates the active job)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "cancel", "queueId": <id>}    -> {"req", "ok": true} (removes a waiting item)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "pause", "paused": <bool>}   -> {"req", "ok": true} (bool=true pauses the active job
                                                          via SIGSTOP, false resumes it via SIGCONT; no-op if the
                                                          job already is / isn't paused)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "reorder", "queueId": <id>,
   "newIndex": <0-based waiting index>}                 -> {"req", "ok": true} (moves a waiting item)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "getQueue"}                   -> {"req", "ok": true, "queue": [...]} (snapshot like the queue event)
  {"req": <id>, "action": "theme"}                      -> {"req", "ok": true, "theme": {...}} (read-only)

The host broadcasts {"req": <id>, "event": "queue", "queue": [...]} (active
item first, then waiting items) on every queue change, plus the per-active-job
stream {"req", "event": "progress"|"info"|"file"|"done"|"error"|"cancelled"}.

Security mirrors the Omarchy host: strict http(s) URL check, output
confinement via realpath, no control characters in echoed strings, nothing
user-controlled is ever shell-interpolated, "--" ends yt-dlp options.
"""
